# Software Defined Networking (SDN)

SDN separates the network control functions from the physical hardware, allowing centralized and programmable network management.

---

# SDN Architecture

## 1. Infrastructure Layer
- Physical and virtual network devices  
- Includes:
  - Switches  
  - Routers  
  - Access points  

### Purpose
- Forwards network traffic  

---

## 2. Control Layer
- Centralized SDN controller  
- Makes routing and forwarding decisions  

### Functions
- Network intelligence  
- Traffic management  
- Policy enforcement  

---

## 3. Application Layer
- Network applications and services  

### Examples
- Monitoring tools  
- Security applications  
- Automation platforms  

---

# SD-LAN (Software Defined LAN)

- Uses centralized management for LAN infrastructure  
- Simplifies network configuration and monitoring  

## Characteristics
- Centralized control  
- Automation  
- Easy scalability  
- Policy-based management  
- Improved visibility  

---

# VXLAN — Virtual Extensible LAN

- Extends Layer 2 networks across Layer 3 infrastructure  
- Used in large data centers and cloud environments  

## Features
- Supports up to 16 million networks  
- Improves scalability over traditional VLANs  

---

# DCI — Data Center Interconnection

- Connects multiple data centers together  

## Purpose
- Disaster recovery  
- Data replication  
- Workload migration  

---

# VLAN vs VXLAN

## VLAN
- Traditional Layer 2 segmentation  
- Limited to 4096 VLANs  

## VXLAN
- Overlay network technology  
- Supports millions of isolated networks  

---

